# Leading slashes matter here — these are gitignore-style patterns, so an
# unanchored "supabase/" would also match src/lib/supabase/ (the actual
# Supabase client code the whole app imports) and break the build. Anchor
# every pattern to the repo root so only the intended top-level folder matches.

# The Vercel CLI tries to upload the whole project directory by default,
# including electron/ (its own node_modules bundles the full Electron/
# Chromium runtime, and electron/dist/ has an 82MB installer built during
# development). None of that belongs in the web app deployment.
/electron/

# Not needed at runtime — migrations are already applied directly to the
# live Supabase project, not deployed as part of the app. NOT src/lib/supabase/.
/supabase/

# Test-only, not needed for the production build.
/tests/
